   a. Butan-1-ol (CH3CH2CH2CH2OH)
   b. Butan-2-ol (CH3CH(OH)CH2CH3)

2. Functional group isomerism: This type of isomerism occurs when the molecule has the same molecular formula but different functional groups. For C4H10O, the possible functional group isomers are:

   a. Butan-1-ol (CH3CH2CH2CH2OH)
   b. Butan-2-ol (CH3CH(OH)CH2CH3)
   c. Butanal (CH3CH2CH2CHO)
   d. Butanone (CH3CH2COCH3)

In summary, the possible isomers for C4H10O are:

1. Butan-1-ol (CH3CH2CH2CH2OH)
2. Butan-2-ol (CH3CH(OH)CH2CH3)
3. Butanal (CH3CH2CH2CHO)
4. Butanone (CH3CH2COCH3)

The differences between these isomers are in their molecular structures, which affect their physical and chemical properties.
