","To determine which sulfides precipitate when \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) is added to the given mixture, we compare the solubility product (\( K_{sp} \)) of the sulfides formed with the sulfide ion concentration. The sulfides with \( K_{sp} \) values less than the sulfide ion concentration will precipitate.

1. **Solubility Products (\( K_{sp} \)) of Sulfides:**
   - \( \text{MnS} \): \( K_{sp} = 10^{-19} \)
   - \( \text{NiS} \): \( K_{sp} = 10^{-21} \)
   - \( \text{CuS} \): \( K_{sp} = 10^{-35} \)
   - \( \text{HgS} \): \( K_{sp} = 10^{-54} \)

2. **Sulfide Ion Concentration:**
   - When \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) is passed into an acidified solution, it forms \( \text{H}_3\text{O}^+ \) and \( \text{S}^{2-} \). The sulfide ion concentration depends on the \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) pressure and the acidity of the solution. For simplicity, assume the sulfide ion concentration is \( 10^{-7} \) M (a typical value for a moderately acidic solution).

3. **Comparison of \( K_{sp} \) and \( [\text{S}^{2-}] \):**
   - \( \text{MnS} \): \( K_{sp} (10^{-19}) > [\text{S}^{2-}] (10^{-7}) \): No precipitation.
   - \( \text{NiS} \): \( K_{sp} (10^{-21}) < [\text{S}^{2-}] (10^{-7}) \): Precipitates.
   - \( \text{CuS} \): \( K_{sp} (10^{-35}) < [\text{S}^{2-}] (10^{-7}) \): Precipitates.
   - \( \text{HgS} \): \( K_{sp} (10^{-54}) < [\text{S}^{2-}] (10^{-7}) \): Precipitates.

4. **Conclusion:**
   The sulfides of \( \text{Ni}^{2+} \), \( \text{Cu}^{2+} \), and \( \text{Hg}^{2+} \) will precipitate when \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) is passed into the given mixture. 

Final Answer: \(\boxed{\text{NiS}, \text{CuS}, \text{HgS}}\)
