The relationship between vapor pressure and PEL is that **liquids with higher vapor pressures typically have lower PELs**. This is because liquids with higher vapor pressures evaporate more readily, increasing the likelihood of higher concentrations of the substance in the air. To maintain a safe exposure level, the PEL must be lower for these substances.  

