   - If \( b \in A \), then \( b \notin (A \setminus B) \), and since \( (A \setminus B) \subseteq A \), we still have \( b \in A \).

4. In both cases, we conclude that \( b \in A \). 

5. Therefore, for any \( b \in B \), \( b \in A \), which implies \( B \subseteq A \).

