   \[
   \text{Rate} = \frac{\text{Total Amount}}{\text{Time}} = \frac{6,000}{5} = 1,200 \text{ per day}
   \]

2. **Determine the new rate of service:**
   \[
   \text{New Rate} = 1,200 + 150 = 1,350 \text{ per day}
   \]

3. **Calculate the new time to complete the service:**
   \[
   \text{New Time} = \frac{\text{Total Amount}}{\text{New Rate}} = \frac{6,000}{1,350} \approx 4.24 \text{ years}
   \]

4. **Round to the nearest whole number:**
   \[
   \text{New Time} \approx 4 \text{ years}
   \]

Thus, the new repayment plan is \(\boxed{4}\) years.
