   \]
   The weight is in newtons.

**Final Answer**:
The weight of the body is:
\[
W = \boxed{0.00012 \left( r_{\text{outer}}^2 - r_{\text{inner}}^2 \right) \, \text{N}}
\]
where \(r_{\text{outer}}\) and \(r_{\text{inner}}\) are the outer and inner radii of the conical duct, respectively.
