The change in internal energy is:
\[
dU = dW = F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v \cdot dt
\]

Thus, the entropy production rate is:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v \cdot dt}{T} = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v}{T}
\]

Therefore, the entropy production rate is \( \boxed{\frac{F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v}{T}} \).

