","The entropy production rate \( \Pi_S \) is given by:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{dU}{T}
\]
where \( dU \) is the change in internal energy of the system.

For the rubbing of hands, the work done by friction converts to heat, which increases the internal energy of the system. The work done by friction is:
\[
dW = F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v \cdot dt
\]
where \( dt \) is the time interval.

The change in internal energy is:
\[
dU = dW = F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v \cdot dt
\]

Thus, the entropy production rate is:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v \cdot dt}{T} = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v}{T}
\]

